{"id": 7, "ts": 1780621104.7172859, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s thorough summary of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s technical strengths, but I\u2019m less convinced that D is the best overall fit. While D does respond adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, and takes responsibility seriously, the notes also flag that D is regarded as arrogant and has relatively weak leadership skills. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, those attitude issues can undermine crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014areas that are just as safety\u2011critical as technical competence.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, is described as very conscientious and handles stress very well, which directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience criterion that we have not yet evaluated for D. B also excels at assessing weather conditions and has excellent computer skills, supporting both operational reliability and technical competence. Although B can be grumpy and occasionally uncooperative, the evidence of strong stress handling and conscientiousness suggests a more reliable and calm performance under the pressures of international flights.\nGiven the balance of strengths and concerns, I would provisionally recommend **Candidate\u202fB** for the long\u2011distance pilot role, pending further clarification on crew\u2011cooperation behaviors for both candidates."}
